WEBVTT

00:02:30.002 --> 00:02:34.313
Our need for a break flies in the face
of our cultural narrative about hustling,

00:02:34.337 --> 00:02:37.128
in other words, the stories
that we as a society

00:02:37.152 --> 00:02:39.518
tell each other
about what success looks like

00:02:39.542 --> 00:02:41.028
and what it takes to get there.

00:02:41.052 --> 00:02:42.728
Stories like the American Dream,

00:02:42.752 --> 00:02:45.648
which is one of our most
deeply rooted beliefs.

00:02:45.672 --> 00:02:48.868
This tells us that if we work hard,
we'll be successful.

00:02:48.892 --> 00:02:50.418
But there's a flip side.

00:02:50.442 --> 00:02:52.328
If you aren't successful,

00:02:52.352 --> 00:02:55.928
it must mean that you're not
working hard enough.

00:02:55.952 --> 00:02:58.218
And if you don't think
you're doing enough,

00:02:58.242 --> 00:03:00.898
of course you're going to stay
late, pull all-nighters